The World Wide Web inventor plans to create a new Internet to compete with Google and Facebook
Tim Berners-Lee is launching a new company that wants to compete with Facebook, Amazon and Google.
One of the most important projects of the world of technology is a company that is based on Berners-Lee open-source open-distance platform.
The Solidarity platform allows users to choose where their data is stored and which people can access certain information.
In an unexclusive interview with Fast Company, Berners-Lee joked that Inrupt's hidden intention was "domurging the world".
“We have to do it now,” he said.
"It's a historic moment."
The app utilizes Solid platform technology to allow users to create their own “Personal Online Data Store”.
It may contain lists of contacts, a list of outstanding tasks, a calendar, a music library and other personal and professional tools.
It’s like Google Drive, Microsoft Outlook, Slack and Spotify. They are all available in a browser at the same time.
The only thing about the online personal data store is that the user is the one who decides who can access certain information.
The company calls it “Personal Empowerment Through Data”.
According to the company’s CEO, John Bruce, “the company integrates adequate resources, processes and aptitudes so that the Solid platform is available to everyone.
The company is currently formed by Berners-Lee, Bruce, a security platform acquired by IBM, a team of developers hired to work on the project, and a community of volunteer co-creators.
As of this week, technology developers from all over the world will be able to create their own decentralized applications using the tools available on the Inrupt website.
Berners-Lee has said that no one in his team is talking about “Facebook” and “Facebook on whether a radical change has to be put in place where all the business models have to be completely emptied during the night.”
"We're not asking for permission."
According to Berners-Lee, “Inrupt of Inrupt is to provide commercial energy and an ecosystem to help protect the integrity and quality of the new integrated website on the Solid platform.”
In 1994, Berners-Lee transformed the Internet when he founded the World Wide Web Consortium at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
Over the past few months, Berners-Lee has been an influential voice in the debate on network neutrality.
At the same time, Berners-Lee will continue to be the Founder and Director of the World Wide Web Consortium, the World Wide Web and the Open Data Institute.
“I’m incredibly optimistic about this new era on the web,” Berners-Lee said.
Bernard Vann: Celebration of the cleric of the Victory Cross
The only cleric in the Church of England who won a Victory Cross during World War I as a combatant has been honoured in his hometown for 100 years.
Lieutenant-Colonel and Reverent Bernard Vann received the award on September 29, 1918 for an attack on Bellenglise and Lehaucourt.
However, he was shot down by a sniper four days later, and he never knew that he had won the most important British military honour.
Their two granddaughters unveiled a commemorative gravestone at a Saturday parade in Rushden, Northamptonshire.
One of his granddaughters, Michael Vann, said that it was "magnificently symbolically symbolic" to be presented exactly 100 years after his granddaughter.
On September 29, 1918, Lieutenant-Colonel Vann led his battalion on the Saint-Quentin Channel, "through a very thick fog and under the heavy fire of guns and machine guns."
He later rushed to the line of fire and, with the "maximum bravery", he marched to the top of the row before jumping on a cannon with a single canoe with a single hand.
Lieutenant-Colonel was shot down by a German sniper on October 4, 1918, just a month before the end of the war.
Michael Vann (72) said that his grandfather’s actions were a feat that could never be the same, resulting in a feeling of humiliation.
He and his brother, James Vann, also left a crown after the parade, led by the Brentwood Imperial Youth Band.
Michael Vann said that he was very honored to be part of the parade and added that the value of a true hero is demonstrated by the support of a lot of people.
