It’s been more than a decade since the Southern District of New York has brought a case of a death penalty.
Khalid Barnes was jailed for the murder of two drug smugglers, but was eventually sentenced to life imprisonment in September 2009.
The last time a death sentence took place in New York City was in 1953 by Julius and Ethel Rosenberg, who had been executed after being convicted of conspiring for espionage during the Cold-West War two years.
